{"id": "sevt_01UdMs5oJRMD3txyiamovgpa", "content": [{"text": "The cause is the cart deploy `df06e76`, which replaced one batched price query with one query per cart line.\n\n**Timeline (UTC)**\n- **14:43:20:** cart deploy `df06e76` (\"price cart lines individually\").\n- **14:43:** cart p99 jumps from about 75 ms to about 3,700 ms, so the gap is under a minute.\n- **14:44\u201314:51:** `db_pool_utilization` climbs steadily from about 0.15 to 0.92.\n- **14:52:** the pool hits 100% (50/50 connections, 12 waiters). Cart starts returning 500s with `PoolTimeout`, at an error rate of roughly 0.1\u20130.75.\n\n**Why it isn't the other deploys**\n- Checkout (14:41) landed before the jump.\n- Auth (14:44:50) landed after the jump had already started.\n\n**Diff**\n- `price_cart()` used to run one `sku_id IN (...)` query and group the results in memory.\n- It now runs `SkuPrice.objects.filter(sku_id=line.sku_id)` inside a loop over the cart lines, so a cart with N lines makes N queries.\n- That is the first item on the runbook's list of things that have burned us.\n\n**Log confirmation**\n- Before 14:43:20, `app.log` has 217 batched `sku_id IN (?)` queries and no per-row ones.\n- After 14:43:20, it has 1,888 per-row `sku_id = ?` queries and no batched ones.\n- Each per-row query takes only about 4\u20137 ms. The slowdown comes from holding connections across many sequential queries per request, not from slow queries.\n- The `PoolTimeout` errors begin at 14:52:11.\n\n**Suggested action:** roll back or revert `df06e76`, or restore the batched `sku_id__in` query.\n\n> **Root cause:** `df06e76` \u2014 `price_cart()` now issues one `SkuPrice` query per cart line instead of one batched `IN` query, which multiplies DB round-trips per request and exhausts cart's 50-connection pool.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T05:56:56.411481Z", "type": "agent.message"}
